message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on portable steel storage units (like Mini-Containers / "Conex"-style or storage sheds). Steel storage sheds are typically classified under 9406.90.00 (prefabricated buildings) — flat-packed, assembled after importation. Steel prefabricated buildings: 9406.90.0030 "Other: Of iron or steel"? Before 2022, 9406.00.80 covered "Other" prefabricated buildings, with 9406.00.8030 for "Of iron or steel"? Current HTSUS: 9406.10 wooden; 9406.20.00 modular building units, of steel; 9406.30.00 modular building units, of concrete; 9406.90 other: 9406.90.0030 "Of iron or steel"? I recall 9406.90.0030 is "Other: Of iron or steel" with 9406.90.0050 for other materials... Actually, 9406.90.00 subdivisions: 9406.90.0010 Greenhouses?; 9406.90.0020 Greenhouses; 9406.90.0030 Of iron or steel; 9406.90.0050 Of aluminum; 9406.90.0090 Other. I believe it's 9406.90.0030 for steel prefabricated buildings.

Alternatively, the units might be classified as containers under 7310 or 8609. A cube with double doors, portable storage units, flat-packed: assembled after import, likely prefabricated building. I'll go with 9406.90.0030.

{"hts_code": "9406.90.0030", "reason": "Flat-packed steel storage units imported for post-importation assembly are prefabricated buildings of iron or steel under heading 9406 (GRI 2(a))."}
